Supplemental Materials for "A Physics-Informed Digital Framework for Low-Cost Pavement Roughness Assessment Using Vehicle-Response Sensing".  This record contains the supplemental material associated with the manuscript &ldquo;A Physics-Informed Digital Framework for Low-Cost Pavement Roughness Assessment Using Vehicle-Response Sensing.&rdquo; 
 The supplemental material comprises Figure S1, which presents representative pavement distress types observed along the study route: (a) alligator cracking, (b) patching, (c) pothole, and (d) transverse cracking. 
 The figure provides visual documentation supporting the pavement condition assessment described in the manuscript.
